Possible scoping fields include:

- Folder hierarchy
- Business unit hierarchy
- Process
- Product
- Risk
- Data domain
- Application
- Existing Payments population rules
- Cross-reference relationships

Before comparing three candidate domains, define a versioned domain-population rule for each candidate.

For every candidate domain, report:

- Inclusion rule
- Included object types
- Number included through each rule
- Overlaps between rules
- Orphaned objects
- Ambiguous objects assigned to several domains
- Objects included only from narrative text
- Estimated precision from a reviewed sample

Do not allow domain membership to become an undocumented filter.

Payments is a plausible candidate because an existing population and related process work are available, but it must still be evaluated using the same scorecard as other candidate domains.

