5. SEPARATE G0 DATA READINESS FROM PILOT ATTRACTIVENESS
======================================================================

Some checks determine whether the data can support the method. Others determine whether a domain is strategically worthwhile.

Keep these separate.

Data-readiness dimensions:

- Narrative usability
- Date validity
- Issue-action linking
- Incident narrative
- Observation history
- Process and application resolution
- Source continuity
- Privacy feasibility

Pilot-attractiveness dimensions:

- Number of material closed issues
- Material incident volume
- Financial and customer consequence
- SME availability
- Existing review forum
- Sponsor commitment
- Decision capacity
- Current difficulty of closure challenge
- Potential to transfer to another domain

A domain may be data-ready but strategically weak.

Another domain may be strategically attractive but fail G0.

The scorecard should show both dimensions rather than combining them into one score.

